"""Cybersecurity glossary, part 21: defence techniques, certificates and email security, incident handling and forensics, privacy techniques, security tools,
and well-known malware families and threat groups (named in public reports, for recognition only).
Row = (id, English name, aliases, category, photo query, local names {fr,sw,rw} or None, en_meaning, en_use, fr_meaning, fr_use, rw_meaning, rw_use, sw_meaning, sw_use)
Awareness-level, protective content. Group attributions are those made by governments and researchers in public reports and are not proof. Kinyarwanda and Kiswahili are a DRAFT for review."""
from cyber_terms_20 import R

TERMS_21 = [
    R("port-knocking", "Port knocking", ["port knock", "knocking sequence"], "network", "locked door with secret knock", {"fr": "Port knocking (frappe de ports)", "sw": "Port knocking", "rw": "Port knocking"},
      ("A technique that keeps a service port closed until the client sends a secret sequence of connection attempts to other ports, after which the firewall opens the port for that client only.", "It hides services such as SSH from scanners, but is an extra layer, not a replacement for strong authentication, updates and a VPN."),
      ("Technique qui garde fermé le port d'un service tant que le client n'a pas envoyé une séquence secrète de tentatives de connexion vers d'autres ports ; le pare-feu ouvre alors le port pour ce seul client.", "Elle masque des services comme SSH aux scanners, mais reste une couche supplémentaire, pas un remplacement de l'authentification forte, des mises à jour et d'un VPN."),
      ("Uburyo bugumisha ifunguye (port) ya serivisi ifunze kugeza umukiliya yohereje urukurikirane rw'ibanga rw'ibigerageza by'ihuzwa ku yandi ma port, hanyuma firewall ikayifungurira uwo mukiliya gusa.", "Buhisha serivisi nka SSH ku bagenzura imiyoboro, ariko ni urwego rwiyongera, si igisimbura kwemeza gukomeye, ivugurura na VPN."),
      ("Mbinu inayoweka port ya huduma imefungwa hadi mteja atume mfuatano wa siri wa majaribio ya muunganisho kwenye port nyingine, kisha firewall hufungua port kwa mteja huyo pekee.", "Huficha huduma kama SSH kutoka kwa skana, lakini ni tabaka la ziada, si mbadala wa uthibitishaji imara, masasisho na VPN.")),
    R("forward-reverse-proxy", "Forward proxy and reverse proxy", ["reverse proxy", "forward proxy", "socks proxy", "proxy types", "vpn tunneling"], "network", "proxy server between client and website", {"fr": "Proxy direct et proxy inverse", "sw": "Forward proxy na reverse proxy", "rw": "Forward proxy na reverse proxy"},
      ("A forward proxy sits in front of users and makes their web requests on their behalf (filtering, caching, hiding the user's address). A reverse proxy sits in front of servers and receives requests for them (load balancing, TLS, a WAF).", "Reverse proxies protect servers by hiding them and filtering attacks; forward proxies enforce an organisation's browsing rules. Neither makes you anonymous to the proxy owner."),
      ("Un proxy direct se place devant les utilisateurs et fait leurs requêtes web à leur place (filtrage, cache, masquage de l'adresse). Un proxy inverse se place devant les serveurs et reçoit les requêtes pour eux (répartition de charge, TLS, WAF).", "Les proxys inverses protègent les serveurs en les cachant et en filtrant les attaques ; les proxys directs appliquent les règles de navigation d'une organisation. Aucun ne vous rend anonyme vis-à-vis de son propriétaire."),
      ("Forward proxy iba imbere y'abakoresha ikabasaba ibyo kuri web mu cyimbo cyabo (filtering, cache, guhisha aderesi). Reverse proxy iba imbere ya seriveri ikakira ibyifuzo mu cyimbo cyazo (kugabanya umutwaro, TLS, WAF).", "Reverse proxy irinda seriveri izihisha kandi ica ibitero; forward proxy ikurikiza amategeko y'ikigo yo gukoresha murandasi. Nta na rimwe rituma utamenyekana kuri nyiraryo."),
      ("Forward proxy huwa mbele ya watumiaji na kufanya maombi yao ya wavuti kwa niaba yao (uchujaji, cache, kuficha anwani). Reverse proxy huwa mbele ya seva na kupokea maombi kwa niaba yao (usambazaji wa mzigo, TLS, WAF).", "Reverse proxy hulinda seva kwa kuzificha na kuchuja mashambulizi; forward proxy hutekeleza kanuni za kuvinjari za shirika. Hakuna inayokufanya usijulikane kwa mmiliki wake.")),
    R("epp", "EPP (endpoint protection platform)", ["endpoint protection platform", "endpoint protection", "epp antivirus", "next-gen antivirus", "ngav"], "operations", "laptop with shield icon", {"fr": "EPP (plateforme de protection des terminaux)", "sw": "EPP (jukwaa la ulinzi wa vifaa)", "rw": "EPP (urubuga rurinda ibikoresho)"},
      ("Software installed on computers and phones that PREVENTS threats: antivirus, anti-malware, firewall, device control and sometimes machine-learning detection. EDR adds recording and investigation after something gets through.", "A basic layer for every device. Modern products combine EPP and EDR in one agent; keep it updated and do not disable it."),
      ("Logiciel installé sur ordinateurs et téléphones qui EMPÊCHE les menaces : antivirus, anti-malware, pare-feu, contrôle des périphériques et parfois détection par apprentissage automatique. L'EDR ajoute l'enregistrement et l'investigation quand quelque chose passe.", "Couche de base pour chaque appareil. Les produits modernes combinent EPP et EDR dans un seul agent ; gardez-le à jour et ne le désactivez pas."),
      ("Porogaramu ishyirwa kuri mudasobwa na telefone IKUMIRA iterabwoba: antivirus, anti-malware, firewall, kugenzura ibikoresho bihujwe rimwe na rimwe no gutahura binyuze mu kwiga kwa mashini. EDR yongeraho kwandika no gukora iperereza iyo hari ibyinjiye.", "Urwego rw'ibanze kuri buri gikoresho. Ibicuruzwa bigezweho bihuza EPP na EDR muri agent imwe; irebe ko igezweho kandi ntuyihagarike."),
      ("Programu iliyosakinishwa kwenye kompyuta na simu inayoZUIA vitisho: antivirus, anti-malware, firewall, udhibiti wa vifaa na wakati mwingine ugunduzi kwa kujifunza kwa mashine. EDR huongeza kurekodi na uchunguzi kitu kikipita.", "Tabaka la msingi kwa kila kifaa. Bidhaa za kisasa huunganisha EPP na EDR katika wakala mmoja; ibakize ikisasishwa na usiizime.")),
    R("iast", "IAST (interactive application security testing)", ["interactive application security testing", "iast testing", "application testing types"], "appsec", "code analysis dashboard", {"fr": "IAST (test interactif de sécurité applicative)", "sw": "IAST", "rw": "IAST"},
      ("A way of testing a running application from the inside: a small agent watches the code while tests or users run it and reports real vulnerabilities with the exact line, mixing the strengths of SAST (code) and DAST (running app).", "Useful in development pipelines to cut false alarms. It still needs good test coverage and must be paired with code review and dependency checks."),
      ("Une façon de tester une application en cours d'exécution de l'intérieur : un petit agent observe le code pendant que des tests ou utilisateurs l'exécutent et signale de vraies vulnérabilités avec la ligne exacte, alliant les forces du SAST (code) et du DAST (application en marche).", "Utile dans les chaînes de développement pour réduire les fausses alertes. Elle exige une bonne couverture de tests et doit s'ajouter aux revues de code et au contrôle des dépendances."),
      ("Uburyo bwo kugerageza porogaramu iri gukora imbere: agent nto ireba code mu gihe ibizamini cyangwa abakoresha bayikoresha ikamenyesha intege nke nyazo n'umurongo nyawo, ihuza imbaraga za SAST (code) na DAST (porogaramu iri gukora).", "Bufasha mu nzira z'iterambere kugabanya impuruza z'ibinyoma. Burakeneye ibizamini byuzuye kandi bugomba guhuzwa n'isuzuma rya code n'iy'amadependency."),
      ("Njia ya kujaribu programu inayoendeshwa kutoka ndani: wakala mdogo hutazama msimbo wakati majaribio au watumiaji wanapoutumia na kuripoti udhaifu halisi na mstari kamili, ukichanganya nguvu za SAST (msimbo) na DAST (programu inayoendeshwa).", "Inafaa katika mifereji ya uundaji kupunguza tahadhari za uongo. Bado inahitaji ufunikaji mzuri wa majaribio na lazima iambatane na ukaguzi wa msimbo na utegemezi.")),
    R("slsa-sigstore", "SLSA, Sigstore and software supply-chain integrity", ["slsa", "sigstore", "cosign", "in-toto", "build provenance", "supply chain levels for software artifacts"], "appsec", "software build pipeline with checks", {"fr": "SLSA, Sigstore et intégrité de la chaîne d'approvisionnement logicielle", "sw": "SLSA, Sigstore na uadilifu wa mnyororo wa ugavi wa programu", "rw": "SLSA, Sigstore n'ubuzima buzima bw'urunigi rwa porogaramu"},
      ("SLSA is a framework of levels that shows how well a software build is protected against tampering, and Sigstore (with tools like cosign) lets developers sign and verify software and containers. Together with an SBOM they prove where software came from and that it was not altered.", "Use signed packages from trusted sources, pin dependency versions, verify signatures and build on locked-down pipelines to reduce supply-chain attacks like SolarWinds."),
      ("SLSA est un cadre de niveaux montrant dans quelle mesure une compilation logicielle est protégée contre la falsification, et Sigstore (avec des outils comme cosign) permet de signer et vérifier logiciels et conteneurs. Avec une SBOM, ils prouvent l'origine d'un logiciel et son intégrité.", "Utilisez des paquets signés de sources fiables, épinglez les versions de dépendances, vérifiez les signatures et compilez sur des chaînes verrouillées pour réduire les attaques de la chaîne d'approvisionnement comme SolarWinds."),
      ("SLSA ni urwego rw'ibipimo rwerekana uko kubaka porogaramu birinzwe kuhindurwa, na Sigstore (hamwe na cosign) bituma abategura basinya bakagenzura porogaramu na containers. Hamwe na SBOM, bigaragaza aho porogaramu yaturutse n'uko itahinduwe.", "Koresha paquets zisinye ziva ahizewe, ushyire verisiyo z'amadependency, ugenzure umukono kandi wubake ku miyoboro ifunze kugira ngo ugabanye ibitero by'urunigi nka SolarWinds."),
      ("SLSA ni mfumo wa viwango unaoonyesha jinsi ujenzi wa programu unavyolindwa dhidi ya kuchezewa, na Sigstore (pamoja na zana kama cosign) huwawezesha wasanidi kusaini na kuthibitisha programu na containers. Pamoja na SBOM, huthibitisha programu ilitoka wapi na haikubadilishwa.", "Tumia vifurushi vilivyosainiwa kutoka vyanzo vinavyoaminika, funga matoleo ya utegemezi, thibitisha saini na ujenge kwenye mifereji iliyofungwa kupunguza mashambulizi ya mnyororo wa ugavi kama SolarWinds.")),
    R("csr-caa-dane", "CSR, CAA records and DANE (certificate controls)", ["csr", "certificate signing request", "caa record", "dane", "dns certificate authority authorization"], "crypto", "digital certificate request form", {"fr": "CSR, enregistrements CAA et DANE", "sw": "CSR, rekodi za CAA na DANE", "rw": "CSR, CAA na DANE"},
      ("A CSR (certificate signing request) is what a website owner sends to a certificate authority to get a certificate. A CAA DNS record states which authorities may issue certificates for a domain, and DANE publishes certificate details in DNSSEC-signed DNS.", "CAA and DANE reduce the risk of fraudulent certificates. Keep private keys secret, monitor Certificate Transparency logs and renew certificates before they expire."),
      ("Une CSR (demande de signature de certificat) est ce qu'un propriétaire de site envoie à une autorité de certification pour obtenir un certificat. Un enregistrement DNS CAA indique quelles autorités peuvent émettre des certificats pour un domaine, et DANE publie les détails du certificat dans un DNS signé DNSSEC.", "CAA et DANE réduisent le risque de faux certificats. Gardez les clés privées secrètes, surveillez les journaux Certificate Transparency et renouvelez les certificats avant expiration."),
      ("CSR (certificate signing request) ni icyo nyir'urubuga yohereza ku kigo gitanga impamyabumenyi (CA) kugira ngo abone icyemezo. CAA ni inyandiko ya DNS ivuga ibigo byemerewe gutanga ibyemezo bya domain, naho DANE itangaza amakuru y'icyemezo muri DNS isinywa na DNSSEC.", "CAA na DANE bigabanya ibyago by'ibyemezo by'impimbano. Bika imfunguzo z'ibanga mu ibanga, ukurikirane Certificate Transparency kandi uvugurure ibyemezo mbere y'uko birangira."),
      ("CSR (ombi la kusainiwa cheti) ndilo mmiliki wa tovuti hutuma kwa mamlaka ya vyeti kupata cheti. Rekodi ya CAA ya DNS hueleza mamlaka zipi zinaruhusiwa kutoa vyeti kwa kikoa, na DANE huchapisha maelezo ya cheti kwenye DNS iliyosainiwa na DNSSEC.", "CAA na DANE hupunguza hatari ya vyeti bandia. Weka funguo za faragha siri, fuatilia kumbukumbu za Certificate Transparency na uhuishe vyeti kabla ya kuisha.")),
    R("dmarc-reports-arc", "DMARC reports and ARC (email authentication in practice)", ["dmarc reporting", "dmarc policy", "arc email", "spf softfail", "dkim selector", "dmarc reject", "dmarc quarantine"], "network", "email authentication report dashboard", {"fr": "Rapports DMARC et ARC", "sw": "Ripoti za DMARC na ARC", "rw": "Raporo za DMARC na ARC"},
      ("DMARC tells receivers what to do with mail that fails SPF/DKIM checks (none, quarantine or reject) and sends reports showing who is sending mail as your domain. ARC preserves the original results when mail is forwarded.", "Start DMARC at 'none' to read reports, fix legitimate senders, then move to quarantine and reject so criminals cannot easily spoof your domain."),
      ("DMARC indique aux destinataires que faire des e-mails qui échouent aux contrôles SPF/DKIM (none, quarantine ou reject) et envoie des rapports montrant qui envoie des e-mails au nom de votre domaine. ARC conserve les résultats d'origine quand un e-mail est transféré.", "Commencez DMARC à « none » pour lire les rapports, corrigez les expéditeurs légitimes, puis passez à quarantine et reject afin que les criminels ne puissent pas facilement usurper votre domaine."),
      ("DMARC ibwira abakira icyo bakora ku imeri itsinzwe n'ibizamini bya SPF/DKIM (none, quarantine cyangwa reject) ikohereza raporo zerekana ubohereza imeri mu izina rya domain yawe. ARC ibika ibisubizo by'ibanze iyo imeri yoherejwe ahandi.", "Tangira DMARC kuri «none» usome raporo, ukosore abohereza nyabo, hanyuma ujye kuri quarantine na reject kugira ngo abagizi ba nabi bataba boroherwa no guhimba domain yawe."),
      ("DMARC huwaambia wapokeaji nini cha kufanya na barua zinazoshindwa ukaguzi wa SPF/DKIM (none, quarantine au reject) na hutuma ripoti zinazoonyesha nani anatuma barua kwa jina la kikoa chako. ARC huhifadhi matokeo ya awali barua inapoelekezwa.", "Anza DMARC kwa 'none' kusoma ripoti, rekebisha watumaji halali, kisha nenda quarantine na reject ili wahalifu wasiweze kughushi kikoa chako kwa urahisi.")),
    R("incident-commander-war-room", "Incident commander and war room", ["incident commander", "war room", "major incident roles", "incident roles", "crisis team"], "operations", "team meeting during cyber incident", {"fr": "Chef de crise (incident commander) et cellule de crise", "sw": "Kamanda wa tukio na chumba cha dharura", "rw": "Umuyobozi w'ibyago na ikipe y'ubutabazi"},
      ("During a serious incident one person, the incident commander, leads decisions and keeps order, while others handle technical work, communication and records in a 'war room' (physical or online). Roles are agreed in advance.", "Clear roles, a contact list, a log of decisions and regular status updates prevent confusion. Practise with tabletop exercises and review lessons afterwards."),
      ("Lors d'un incident grave, une personne, le chef de crise (incident commander), conduit les décisions et maintient l'ordre, tandis que d'autres gèrent le technique, la communication et les traces dans une « cellule de crise » (physique ou en ligne). Les rôles sont convenus à l'avance.", "Des rôles clairs, une liste de contacts, un journal des décisions et des points d'étape réguliers évitent la confusion. Entraînez-vous par des exercices sur table et tirez les leçons ensuite."),
      ("Mu gihe cy'ikibazo gikomeye umuntu umwe, umuyobozi w'ibyago (incident commander), ayobora ibyemezo agakomeza gahunda, abandi bakita ku bya tekiniki, itumanaho n'inyandiko mu «cyumba cy'ubutabazi» (kuri interineti cyangwa kigaragara). Inshingano zemeranywa mbere.", "Inshingano zisobanutse, urutonde rw'abahamagarwa, igitabo cy'ibyemezo n'amakuru y'uko ibintu bimeze buri gihe birinda urujijo. Itoze n'imyitozo ku meza kandi usuzume amasomo nyuma."),
      ("Wakati wa tukio kubwa mtu mmoja, kamanda wa tukio (incident commander), huongoza maamuzi na kudumisha utaratibu, huku wengine wakishughulikia kazi ya kiufundi, mawasiliano na kumbukumbu katika 'chumba cha dharura' (halisi au mtandaoni). Majukumu hukubaliwa mapema.", "Majukumu wazi, orodha ya mawasiliano, kumbukumbu ya maamuzi na taarifa za hali za mara kwa mara huzuia mkanganyiko. Fanya mazoezi ya mezani na kagua mafunzo baadaye.")),
    R("forensic-readiness-legal-hold", "Forensic readiness, legal hold and e-discovery", ["forensic readiness", "legal hold", "e-discovery", "ediscovery", "evidence preservation", "preserving evidence"], "operations", "evidence box and legal documents", {"fr": "Préparation forensique, conservation légale et e-discovery", "sw": "Utayari wa uchunguzi wa kidijitali, legal hold na e-discovery", "rw": "Kwitegura iperereza rya digitale, legal hold na e-discovery"},
      ("Forensic readiness means preparing in advance (logs kept long enough, clocks in sync, evidence-handling procedures) so that an investigation can succeed. A legal hold stops deletion of relevant data, and e-discovery is finding and producing electronic records for legal cases.", "Preserve evidence first: do not wipe or 'clean up' affected devices, record who touched what and when, and involve legal and forensic specialists early."),
      ("La préparation forensique consiste à se préparer à l'avance (journaux conservés assez longtemps, horloges synchronisées, procédures de gestion des preuves) pour qu'une enquête puisse aboutir. Une conservation légale empêche la suppression des données utiles, et l'e-discovery consiste à retrouver et produire des documents électroniques pour des affaires juridiques.", "Préservez d'abord les preuves : n'effacez pas et ne « nettoyez » pas les appareils touchés, notez qui a touché quoi et quand, et impliquez tôt juristes et spécialistes forensiques."),
      ("Kwitegura iperereza rya digitale ni ugutegura mbere (logs zibitswe igihe gihagije, amasaha ahuye, uburyo bwo gufata ibimenyetso) kugira ngo iperereza ryitabweho. Legal hold ibuza gusiba amakuru afitanye isano, naho e-discovery ni ugushaka no gutanga inyandiko za elegitoronike mu manza.", "Banza ubike ibimenyetso: ntusibe cyangwa ngo «usukure» ibikoresho byagizweho ingaruka, wandike uwakozeho icyo n'igihe, kandi ushyiremo abanyamategeko n'impuguke z'iperereza hakiri kare."),
      ("Utayari wa uchunguzi wa kidijitali ni kujiandaa mapema (kumbukumbu zilizohifadhiwa muda wa kutosha, saa zilizolingana, taratibu za kushughulikia ushahidi) ili uchunguzi uweze kufaulu. Legal hold huzuia kufutwa kwa data husika, na e-discovery ni kutafuta na kutoa rekodi za kielektroniki kwa kesi za kisheria.", "Hifadhi ushahidi kwanza: usifute wala 'kusafisha' vifaa vilivyoathirika, andika nani aligusa nini na lini, na washirikishe wanasheria na wataalamu wa uchunguzi mapema.")),
    R("network-forensics-timeline", "Network forensics, timeline analysis and log correlation", ["network forensics", "timeline analysis", "log correlation", "packet capture analysis", "pcap analysis", "event correlation"], "operations", "timeline of events on a screen", {"fr": "Forensique réseau, analyse de chronologie et corrélation de journaux", "sw": "Uchunguzi wa mtandao, uchambuzi wa mpangilio wa matukio na uunganishaji wa kumbukumbu", "rw": "Iperereza ry'umuyoboro, isesengura ry'uko ibintu byakurikiranye no guhuza logs"},
      ("Investigators rebuild what happened by analysing captured network traffic (PCAP), building a timeline of events across devices and correlating logs from many systems to connect small clues into one story.", "It works only if clocks are synchronised and logs are kept and protected. SIEM tools automate correlation; humans still judge what it means."),
      ("Les enquêteurs reconstituent ce qui s'est passé en analysant le trafic réseau capturé (PCAP), en construisant une chronologie des événements entre appareils et en corrélant les journaux de nombreux systèmes pour relier de petits indices en une histoire.", "Cela ne marche que si les horloges sont synchronisées et les journaux conservés et protégés. Les SIEM automatisent la corrélation ; l'humain juge encore ce que cela signifie."),
      ("Abakora iperereza bongera kubaka ibyabaye basesengura amakuru y'umuyoboro yafashwe (PCAP), bakubaka uko ibintu byakurikiranye ku bikoresho byinshi kandi bagahuza logs za sisitemu nyinshi kugira ngo bahuze ibimenyetso bito mu nkuru imwe.", "Bikora gusa iyo amasaha ahuye kandi logs zibitswe kandi zirinzwe. SIEM zikora guhuza ku buryo bwikora; abantu baracyasuzuma icyo bivuze."),
      ("Wachunguzi hujenga upya kilichotokea kwa kuchambua trafiki ya mtandao iliyonaswa (PCAP), kujenga mpangilio wa matukio kwenye vifaa na kuunganisha kumbukumbu za mifumo mingi kuunganisha vidokezo vidogo kuwa hadithi moja.", "Inafanya kazi tu ikiwa saa zimelingana na kumbukumbu zimehifadhiwa na kulindwa. SIEM huendesha uunganishaji kiotomatiki; binadamu bado huamua maana yake.")),
    R("takedown", "Takedown (removing malicious sites and content)", ["takedown request", "phishing takedown", "domain takedown", "abuse report", "report phishing site"], "operations", "report abuse button on a website", {"fr": "Retrait (takedown) de sites et contenus malveillants", "sw": "Takedown (kuondoa tovuti na maudhui hasidi)", "rw": "Takedown (gukuraho imbuga n'ibikubiyemo bibi)"},
      ("A takedown is getting a harmful site, account or file removed by asking the host, domain registrar, platform or national CERT (using an abuse report with evidence).", "Report phishing and scams to the brand being imitated, the platform and the national authority; keep screenshots and the full link. Faster removal protects other victims."),
      ("Un takedown consiste à faire retirer un site, compte ou fichier nuisible en le demandant à l'hébergeur, au bureau d'enregistrement du domaine, à la plateforme ou au CERT national (par un signalement d'abus avec preuves).", "Signalez hameçonnage et arnaques à la marque imitée, à la plateforme et à l'autorité nationale ; gardez captures d'écran et lien complet. Un retrait rapide protège d'autres victimes."),
      ("Takedown ni ugutuma urubuga, konti cyangwa dosiye bibi bikurwaho usabye umucumbikira, ikigo cyandika domain, urubuga cyangwa CERT y'igihugu (ukoresheje raporo y'ihohoterwa ifite ibimenyetso).", "Menyesha phishing n'uburiganya ku kigo cyiganwa, ku rubuga no ku buyobozi bw'igihugu; bika screenshots n'link yuzuye. Gukurwaho vuba birinda izindi nzirakarengane."),
      ("Takedown ni kuomba tovuti, akaunti au faili hasidi iondolewe kwa kumwomba mwenyeji, msajili wa kikoa, jukwaa au CERT ya taifa (kwa ripoti ya matumizi mabaya yenye ushahidi).", "Ripoti hadaa na utapeli kwa chapa inayoigwa, jukwaa na mamlaka ya taifa; hifadhi picha za skrini na kiungo kamili. Kuondolewa haraka huwalinda waathirika wengine.")),
    R("anonymisation-pseudonymisation", "Anonymisation, pseudonymisation, k-anonymity and differential privacy", ["pseudonymisation", "pseudonymization", "anonymisation", "anonymization", "k-anonymity", "differential privacy", "de-identification", "re-identification"], "privacy", "data table with names hidden", {"fr": "Anonymisation, pseudonymisation, k-anonymat et confidentialité différentielle", "sw": "Kuficha utambulisho, k-anonymity na faragha tofauti", "rw": "Guhisha umwirondoro, k-anonymity na differential privacy"},
      ("Pseudonymisation replaces names with codes but can be reversed with a key; anonymisation removes identification so it cannot be reversed. k-anonymity makes each person look like at least k-1 others, and differential privacy adds carefully measured random noise to statistics so no single person's data can be inferred.", "Used to share data for research safely. True anonymisation is hard (people can be re-identified by combining datasets), so treat pseudonymised data as personal data."),
      ("La pseudonymisation remplace les noms par des codes mais peut être inversée avec une clé ; l'anonymisation supprime l'identification de façon irréversible. Le k-anonymat fait ressembler chaque personne à au moins k-1 autres, et la confidentialité différentielle ajoute un bruit aléatoire mesuré aux statistiques pour qu'on ne puisse déduire les données d'une personne.", "Servent à partager des données pour la recherche en sécurité. La vraie anonymisation est difficile (on peut réidentifier en croisant des jeux de données) : traitez les données pseudonymisées comme des données personnelles."),
      ("Pseudonymisation isimbuza amazina kode ariko ishobora gusubizwa inyuma n'urufunguzo; anonymisation ikuraho umwirondoro ku buryo budasubira. k-anonymity ituma buri muntu asa nibura n'abandi k-1, naho differential privacy yongeramo urusaku rudasobanutse rupimye ku mibare kugira ngo amakuru y'umuntu umwe adashobora kumenyekana.", "Bikoreshwa mu gusangira amakuru y'ubushakashatsi mu mutekano. Anonymisation nyayo iragoye (abantu bashobora kongera kumenyekana bahuje amakuru), bityo amakuru yahinduwe pseudonym uyafate nk'amakuru bwite."),
      ("Pseudonymisation hubadilisha majina kuwa misimbo lakini inaweza kurudishwa kwa ufunguo; anonymisation huondoa utambulisho kabisa. k-anonymity hufanya kila mtu aonekane kama angalau wengine k-1, na differential privacy huongeza kelele nasibu iliyopimwa kwenye takwimu ili data ya mtu mmoja isiweze kukisiwa.", "Hutumika kushiriki data kwa utafiti kwa usalama. Anonymisation halisi ni ngumu (watu wanaweza kutambuliwa upya kwa kuchanganya seti za data), kwa hiyo chukulia data ya pseudonym kama data binafsi.")),
    R("dsar", "Data subject access request (DSAR) and data rights", ["dsar", "data subject access request", "right of access", "right to erasure", "right to be forgotten", "subject access request"], "privacy", "person requesting their data", {"fr": "Demande d'accès de la personne concernée (DSAR) et droits sur les données", "sw": "Ombi la mhusika wa data (DSAR) na haki za data", "rw": "Ubusabe bw'nyir'amakuru (DSAR) n'uburenganzira ku makuru"},
      ("People may ask an organisation what personal data it holds about them, why, and with whom it is shared (a DSAR), and may ask for corrections or deletion. Laws such as GDPR and Rwanda's Law No 058/2021 give such rights, with limits and deadlines.", "Organisations need to know where personal data is stored and have a procedure to answer. If you make a request, write it clearly, say what you want and keep a copy."),
      ("Toute personne peut demander à un organisme quelles données personnelles il détient sur elle, pourquoi et avec qui elles sont partagées (DSAR), et demander correction ou suppression. Des lois comme le RGPD et la loi rwandaise n° 058/2021 donnent ces droits, avec limites et délais.", "Les organismes doivent savoir où sont stockées les données et avoir une procédure pour répondre. Si vous faites une demande, rédigez-la clairement, précisez ce que vous voulez et gardez une copie."),
      ("Umuntu ashobora gusaba ikigo amakuru bwite kimufiteho, impamvu n'abo asangirwa na bo (DSAR), no gusaba gukosorwa cyangwa gusibwa. Amategeko nka GDPR n'Itegeko n° 058/2021 ry'u Rwanda atanga ubwo burenganzira, hari imbibi n'igihe ntarengwa.", "Ibigo bigomba kumenya aho amakuru bwite abitswe no kugira uburyo bwo gusubiza. Niba usaba, andika neza, vuga ibyo ushaka kandi ubike kopi."),
      ("Mtu anaweza kuomba shirika data binafsi linazoshikilia kumhusu, kwa nini, na nani zinashirikiwa (DSAR), na kuomba marekebisho au kufutwa. Sheria kama GDPR na Sheria Na. 058/2021 ya Rwanda hutoa haki hizo, zikiwa na mipaka na muda.", "Mashirika yanahitaji kujua data binafsi huhifadhiwa wapi na kuwa na utaratibu wa kujibu. Ukiomba, andika wazi, sema unachotaka na hifadhi nakala.")),
    R("secret-sharing-mpc", "Secret sharing and secure multiparty computation", ["secret sharing", "shamir secret sharing", "shamir", "multiparty computation", "mpc", "threshold cryptography"], "crypto", "key split into pieces held by several people", {"fr": "Partage de secret et calcul multipartite sécurisé", "sw": "Kugawa siri na hesabu salama ya pande nyingi", "rw": "Gusangira ibanga na MPC"},
      ("Secret sharing (for example Shamir's scheme) splits a secret key into several pieces so that a minimum number of them (a threshold, like 3 of 5) must be combined to rebuild it. Secure multiparty computation lets several parties compute a result together without revealing their private inputs.", "Used to protect master keys and crypto wallets so that no single person or stolen device can open them, and for private joint analysis."),
      ("Le partage de secret (par exemple le schéma de Shamir) découpe une clé secrète en plusieurs parts dont un nombre minimum (un seuil, comme 3 sur 5) doit être réuni pour la reconstituer. Le calcul multipartite sécurisé permet à plusieurs parties de calculer un résultat sans révéler leurs données privées.", "Utilisé pour protéger clés maîtresses et portefeuilles crypto afin qu'aucune personne ni appareil volé ne puisse les ouvrir seul, et pour des analyses communes privées."),
      ("Gusangira ibanga (urugero uburyo bwa Shamir) bigabanya urufunguzo rw'ibanga mu bice byinshi kandi hakenerwa umubare muto (3 kuri 5) w'ibyo bice kugira ngo rwongere kubakwa. MPC ituma impande nyinshi zibara igisubizo hamwe nta kugaragaza amakuru yazo bwite.", "Bikoreshwa kurinda imfunguzo nkuru na crypto wallets kugira ngo nta muntu umwe cyangwa igikoresho cyibwe gishobora kuzifungura, no mu isesengura rusange ry'ibanga."),
      ("Kugawa siri (mfano mpango wa Shamir) hugawanya ufunguo wa siri kuwa vipande kadhaa ambapo idadi ndogo (kizingiti, kama 3 kati ya 5) lazima ziunganishwe kuujenga upya. Hesabu salama ya pande nyingi huziruhusu pande kadhaa kukokotoa matokeo pamoja bila kufichua data zao za faragha.", "Hutumika kulinda funguo kuu na pochi za crypto ili mtu mmoja au kifaa kilichoibwa kisiweze kuzifungua peke yake, na kwa uchambuzi wa pamoja wa faragha.")),
    R("merkle-tree", "Merkle tree", ["merkle", "hash tree", "merkle hash tree"], "crypto", "tree of hashes diagram", {"fr": "Arbre de Merkle", "sw": "Mti wa Merkle", "rw": "Igiti cya Merkle"},
      ("A tree of hashes in which each leaf is the hash of a piece of data and each parent is the hash of its children, ending in one 'root' hash. Changing any data changes the root, so integrity can be checked quickly.", "Used in blockchains, Git, Certificate Transparency and file-sync systems to prove that data has not been altered without comparing everything."),
      ("Un arbre de hachages où chaque feuille est le hachage d'un morceau de données et chaque parent le hachage de ses enfants, jusqu'à un seul hachage « racine ». Modifier une donnée change la racine, ce qui permet de vérifier rapidement l'intégrité.", "Utilisé dans les blockchains, Git, Certificate Transparency et la synchronisation de fichiers pour prouver que des données n'ont pas été altérées sans tout comparer."),
      ("Igiti cya hashes aho buri kibabi ari hash y'agace k'amakuru na buri mubyeyi ari hash y'abana be, bikarangira kuri hash imwe «ishami rikuru». Guhindura amakuru ayo ari yo yose bihindura iryo shami, bityo ubuziranenge bukagenzurwa vuba.", "Bikoreshwa muri blockchains, Git, Certificate Transparency no mu guhuza dosiye kugira ngo hagaragazwe ko amakuru atahindutse nta gereranya byose."),
      ("Mti wa hashes ambapo kila jani ni hash ya kipande cha data na kila mzazi ni hash ya watoto wake, ukiishia kwenye hash moja 'mzizi'. Kubadilisha data yoyote hubadilisha mzizi, hivyo uadilifu unaweza kukaguliwa haraka.", "Hutumika katika blockchains, Git, Certificate Transparency na mifumo ya kusawazisha faili kuthibitisha data haijabadilishwa bila kulinganisha kila kitu.")),
    R("ransomware-groups", "Well-known ransomware groups (LockBit, Conti, REvil, BlackCat, Clop)", ["lockbit", "conti", "revil", "darkside", "blackcat", "alphv", "clop", "royal ransomware", "ransomware gangs", "ransomware groups"], "attacks", "ransom note on a locked screen", {"fr": "Groupes de rançongiciels connus (LockBit, Conti, REvil...)", "sw": "Makundi maarufu ya ransomware", "rw": "Amatsinda azwi ya ransomware"},
      ("Ransomware is run by organised gangs, often as ransomware-as-a-service where 'affiliates' do the attacks and share profits. Names from public reports include LockBit, Conti, REvil (Sodinokibi), DarkSide, BlackCat (ALPHV) and Clop. Groups split, rebrand and are disrupted by police.", "Names change, the defence does not: offline tested backups, patching, MFA, limiting admin rights, email filtering and a rehearsed response plan. Paying does not guarantee recovery."),
      ("Les rançongiciels sont exploités par des gangs organisés, souvent en ransomware-as-a-service où des « affiliés » mènent les attaques et partagent les profits. Des rapports publics citent LockBit, Conti, REvil (Sodinokibi), DarkSide, BlackCat (ALPHV) et Clop. Les groupes se scindent, changent de nom et sont perturbés par la police.", "Les noms changent, pas la défense : sauvegardes hors ligne testées, correctifs, MFA, droits admin limités, filtrage des e-mails et plan de réponse répété. Payer ne garantit pas la récupération."),
      ("Ransomware iyoborwa n'amatsinda ateguye, kenshi nka ransomware-as-a-service aho «abafatanyabikorwa» bateza ibitero bagasangira inyungu. Amazina avugwa muri raporo rusange: LockBit, Conti, REvil (Sodinokibi), DarkSide, BlackCat (ALPHV) na Clop. Amatsinda arasaranganya, agahindura amazina kandi agahungabanywa na polisi.", "Amazina ariahinduka, uburyo bwo kwirinda ntibuhinduka: backups zitari kuri interineti zagerageje, ivugurura, MFA, kugabanya uburenganzira bwa admin, filtering y'imeri na gahunda y'igisubizo yitorejwe. Kwishyura ntibyemeza gusubirana."),
      ("Ransomware huendeshwa na magenge yaliyopangwa, mara nyingi kama ransomware-as-a-service ambapo 'washirika' hufanya mashambulizi na kugawana faida. Majina kutoka ripoti za umma: LockBit, Conti, REvil (Sodinokibi), DarkSide, BlackCat (ALPHV) na Clop. Makundi hugawanyika, hubadili majina na hufadhaishwa na polisi.", "Majina hubadilika, ulinzi haubadiliki: nakala rudufu nje ya mtandao zilizojaribiwa, masasisho, MFA, kupunguza haki za admin, uchujaji wa barua pepe na mpango wa mwitikio uliofanyiwa mazoezi. Kulipa hakuhakikishi kurejesha.")),
    R("apt-groups", "Well-known APT groups and state-linked actors (APT28, APT29, Lazarus)", ["apt28", "apt29", "fancy bear", "cozy bear", "lazarus group", "apt groups", "state sponsored hackers", "nation state hackers", "sandworm", "scattered spider", "lapsus"], "attacks", "world map with cyber threat markers", {"fr": "Groupes APT connus et acteurs liés à des États", "sw": "Makundi maarufu ya APT na watendaji wanaohusishwa na mataifa", "rw": "Amatsinda azwi ya APT n'abakorera ibihugu"},
      ("Security researchers and governments track long-running, well-resourced groups under names such as APT28 ('Fancy Bear'), APT29 ('Cozy Bear'), Sandworm and Lazarus Group, often linked in public reports to states. Some criminal groups, like Scattered Spider or LAPSUS$, rely on social engineering rather than advanced tools.", "Attribution is difficult and only an estimate. For ordinary people and small organisations the practical defences are the same: MFA, updates, phishing awareness, least privilege and monitoring."),
      ("Chercheurs et gouvernements suivent des groupes durables et bien dotés sous des noms comme APT28 (« Fancy Bear »), APT29 (« Cozy Bear »), Sandworm et Lazarus Group, souvent liés à des États dans des rapports publics. Certains groupes criminels, comme Scattered Spider ou LAPSUS$, misent sur l'ingénierie sociale plutôt que sur des outils avancés.", "L'attribution est difficile et reste une estimation. Pour les particuliers et petites organisations, les défenses pratiques sont les mêmes : MFA, mises à jour, vigilance anti-hameçonnage, moindre privilège et surveillance."),
      ("Abashakashatsi n'ibihugu bakurikirana amatsinda amaze igihe kirekire afite ubushobozi mu mazina nka APT28 («Fancy Bear»), APT29 («Cozy Bear»), Sandworm na Lazarus Group, kenshi ahuzwa n'ibihugu muri raporo rusange. Andi matsinda y'abagizi ba nabi, nka Scattered Spider cyangwa LAPSUS$, yishingikiriza kuri social engineering aho gukoresha ibikoresho bihanitse.", "Kuvuga uwabikoze biragoye kandi ni igereranyo. Ku bantu basanzwe n'ibigo bito uburyo bwo kwirinda ni bumwe: MFA, ivugurura, kuba maso kuri phishing, least privilege no gukurikirana."),
      ("Watafiti na serikali hufuatilia makundi ya muda mrefu yenye rasilimali chini ya majina kama APT28 ('Fancy Bear'), APT29 ('Cozy Bear'), Sandworm na Lazarus Group, mara nyingi yanahusishwa na mataifa kwenye ripoti za umma. Baadhi ya makundi ya wahalifu, kama Scattered Spider au LAPSUS$, hutegemea ulaghai wa kijamii kuliko zana za hali ya juu.", "Kutaja nani alifanya ni vigumu na ni makadirio tu. Kwa watu wa kawaida na mashirika madogo ulinzi wa vitendo ni ule ule: MFA, masasisho, tahadhari dhidi ya hadaa, haki ndogo na ufuatiliaji.")),
    R("trojan-loader-families", "Banking trojan and loader families (Zeus, TrickBot, QakBot, Dridex, Emotet)", ["zeus trojan", "zeus", "trickbot", "qakbot", "qbot", "dridex", "banking trojans", "malware families"], "malware", "malware family names list", {"fr": "Familles de chevaux de Troie bancaires et chargeurs", "sw": "Familia za trojan za benki na loaders", "rw": "Imiryango ya trojan za banki na loaders"},
      ("Some malware families became famous: Zeus (stole online-banking logins), TrickBot, QakBot and Dridex (banking trojans that also load other malware, often leading to ransomware) and Emotet (a spam-delivered loader). Many were taken down or changed form but their methods continue.", "Defence: do not open unexpected attachments, block macros, keep systems patched, use EDR, enable MFA on banking and never save banking passwords in the browser."),
      ("Certaines familles de malwares sont devenues célèbres : Zeus (vol d'identifiants bancaires en ligne), TrickBot, QakBot et Dridex (chevaux de Troie bancaires qui chargent aussi d'autres malwares, menant souvent à un rançongiciel) et Emotet (chargeur diffusé par spam). Beaucoup ont été démantelés ou ont changé de forme mais leurs méthodes perdurent.", "Défense : n'ouvrez pas de pièces jointes inattendues, bloquez les macros, corrigez les systèmes, utilisez un EDR, activez la MFA bancaire et n'enregistrez jamais vos mots de passe bancaires dans le navigateur."),
      ("Imiryango imwe ya malware yamenyekanye: Zeus (yibaga amagambo yo kwinjira kuri banki), TrickBot, QakBot na Dridex (trojan za banki zinashyiraho izindi malware, kenshi zigatera ransomware) na Emotet (loader yoherezwa muri spam). Myinshi yarahagaritswe cyangwa yahinduye isura ariko uburyo bwayo burakomeza.", "Kwirinda: ntufungure dosiye zitateganyijwe, ubuze macros, uvugurure sisitemu, ukoreshe EDR, ufungure MFA kuri banki kandi ntuzigere ubika amagambo y'ibanga ya banki mu rubuga."),
      ("Familia kadhaa za programu hasidi zilijulikana: Zeus (iliiba taarifa za kuingia benki mtandaoni), TrickBot, QakBot na Dridex (trojan za benki zinazopakia programu hasidi nyingine, mara nyingi zikisababisha ransomware) na Emotet (loader inayosambazwa kwa spam). Nyingi zilizimwa au kubadilika lakini mbinu zao zinaendelea.", "Ulinzi: usifungue viambatisho visivyotarajiwa, zuia macros, sasisha mifumo, tumia EDR, washa MFA ya benki na kamwe usihifadhi nywila za benki kwenye kivinjari.")),
    R("stealer-rat-families", "Infostealer and RAT families (RedLine, Raccoon, Lumma, Agent Tesla, njRAT, AsyncRAT, Remcos)", ["redline stealer", "raccoon stealer", "lumma", "agent tesla", "formbook", "njrat", "asyncrat", "remcos", "infostealer families", "rat families"], "malware", "stolen passwords being sold", {"fr": "Familles de voleurs d'informations et de RAT", "sw": "Familia za infostealer na RAT", "rw": "Imiryango ya infostealer na RAT"},
      ("Infostealers such as RedLine, Raccoon, Lumma, Agent Tesla and FormBook steal saved passwords, cookies, crypto wallets and files and sell them as 'logs'. Remote access trojans such as njRAT, AsyncRAT and Remcos give a criminal control of the computer, camera and keyboard.", "Defence: do not install cracked software or unknown 'tools', download only from official sources, use a password manager instead of browser-saved passwords, turn on MFA and rotate passwords after any suspected infection."),
      ("Des voleurs d'informations comme RedLine, Raccoon, Lumma, Agent Tesla et FormBook dérobent mots de passe enregistrés, cookies, portefeuilles crypto et fichiers, et les vendent en « logs ». Des chevaux de Troie d'accès à distance comme njRAT, AsyncRAT et Remcos donnent au criminel le contrôle de l'ordinateur, de la caméra et du clavier.", "Défense : n'installez pas de logiciels piratés ni d'« outils » inconnus, téléchargez depuis des sources officielles, utilisez un gestionnaire de mots de passe plutôt que le navigateur, activez la MFA et changez vos mots de passe après toute infection suspectée."),
      ("Infostealers nka RedLine, Raccoon, Lumma, Agent Tesla na FormBook zibiba amagambo y'ibanga abitswe, cookies, crypto wallets na dosiye zikazigurisha nka «logs». RAT nka njRAT, AsyncRAT na Remcos ziha umugizi wa nabi kugenzura mudasobwa, kamera na keyboard.", "Kwirinda: ntushyireho porogaramu zangijwe (cracked) cyangwa «ibikoresho» bitazwi, kuramo ahemewe gusa, ukoreshe password manager aho gukoresha ibyabitswe mu rubuga, ufungure MFA kandi uhindure amagambo y'ibanga nyuma ya infection ikekwa."),
      ("Infostealers kama RedLine, Raccoon, Lumma, Agent Tesla na FormBook huiba nywila zilizohifadhiwa, cookies, pochi za crypto na faili na kuziuza kama 'logs'. RAT kama njRAT, AsyncRAT na Remcos humpa mhalifu udhibiti wa kompyuta, kamera na kibodi.", "Ulinzi: usisakinishe programu zilizovunjwa (cracked) au 'zana' zisizojulikana, pakua kutoka vyanzo rasmi tu, tumia password manager badala ya nywila zilizohifadhiwa kwenye kivinjari, washa MFA na ubadilishe nywila baada ya maambukizi yanayoshukiwa.")),
    R("notpetya", "NotPetya", ["notpetya", "petya", "not petya", "petya wiper"], "malware", "global shipping and companies disrupted by malware", {"fr": "NotPetya", "sw": "NotPetya", "rw": "NotPetya"},
      ("A 2017 destructive attack that looked like ransomware but was really a wiper: it spread through a booby-trapped update of Ukrainian accounting software and then across company networks worldwide, causing billions of dollars in damage.", "Lessons: supply-chain compromise is real, flat networks let malware spread, backups must be offline and tested, and patching (for example against EternalBlue) matters."),
      ("Une attaque destructrice de 2017 qui ressemblait à un rançongiciel mais était en réalité un wiper : elle s'est propagée via une mise à jour piégée d'un logiciel de comptabilité ukrainien puis sur les réseaux d'entreprises du monde entier, causant des milliards de dollars de dégâts.", "Leçons : la compromission de la chaîne d'approvisionnement est réelle, les réseaux à plat laissent le malware se propager, les sauvegardes doivent être hors ligne et testées, et les correctifs (par exemple contre EternalBlue) comptent."),
      ("Igitero cyo mu 2017 cyangiza cyasaga na ransomware ariko cyari wiper: cyakwirakwiriye binyuze mu ivugurura ryashyizwemo ikintu cy'ubugome rya porogaramu y'ibaruramari ya Ukraine hanyuma ku miyoboro y'ibigo ku isi hose, gitera igihombo cy'ibiliyaridi by'amadolari.", "Amasomo: guhungabanya urunigi rw'ibitangwa ni ukuri, imiyoboro idatandukanyijwe yemerera malware gukwirakwira, backups zigomba kuba zitari kuri interineti kandi zageragejwe, kandi ivugurura (urugero kuri EternalBlue) ni ingenzi."),
      ("Shambulio la uharibifu la 2017 lililoonekana kama ransomware lakini kwa kweli lilikuwa wiper: lilisambaa kupitia sasisho lililotegwa la programu ya uhasibu ya Ukraine kisha kwenye mitandao ya kampuni duniani kote, likisababisha hasara ya mabilioni ya dola.", "Funzo: kuvamia mnyororo wa ugavi ni kweli, mitandao isiyogawanywa huruhusu programu hasidi kusambaa, nakala rudufu lazima ziwe nje ya mtandao na zilizojaribiwa, na masasisho (mfano dhidi ya EternalBlue) ni muhimu.")),
    R("security-tools-by-job", "Security tools by job (Splunk, ELK, Wazuh, ZAP, sqlmap, Velociraptor)", ["splunk", "elk stack", "elastic siem", "wazuh", "ossec", "qradar", "microsoft sentinel", "crowdstrike", "owasp zap", "sqlmap", "velociraptor", "thehive", "security tools list", "tools used by security engineers"], "operations", "security operations dashboard", {"fr": "Outils de sécurité par métier", "sw": "Zana za usalama kulingana na kazi", "rw": "Ibikoresho by'umutekano ukurikije umurimo"},
      ("Defenders use different tools for different jobs: SIEM and log analysis (Splunk, Elastic/ELK, Wazuh, OSSEC, IBM QRadar, Microsoft Sentinel), endpoint protection and response (CrowdStrike, Microsoft Defender, Velociraptor for forensics), case and response handling (TheHive, SOAR platforms) and application testing (OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite; sqlmap tests for SQL injection on systems you are authorised to test).", "Tools help but do not replace skills and process. Only test systems you own or have written permission to test; unauthorised scanning can be illegal."),
      ("Les défenseurs utilisent des outils selon les tâches : SIEM et journaux (Splunk, Elastic/ELK, Wazuh, OSSEC, QRadar, Sentinel), terminaux (CrowdStrike, Defender, Velociraptor), gestion de la réponse (TheHive, SOAR) et tests d'applications (OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite, sqlmap sur des systèmes autorisés).", "Les outils aident mais ne remplacent ni compétences ni processus. Ne testez que des systèmes qui vous appartiennent ou avec autorisation écrite ; un scan non autorisé peut être illégal."),
      ("Abarinzi bakoresha ibikoresho bitandukanye ku murimo utandukanye: SIEM no gusesengura logs (Splunk, Elastic/ELK, Wazuh, OSSEC, IBM QRadar, Microsoft Sentinel), kurinda no gusubiza ku bikoresho (CrowdStrike, Microsoft Defender, Velociraptor mu iperereza), gucunga ibibazo n'ibisubizo (TheHive, SOAR) no kugerageza porogaramu (OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite; sqlmap igerageza SQL injection kuri sisitemu wemerewe kugerageza).", "Ibikoresho birafasha ariko ntibisimbura ubumenyi na gahunda. Gerageza gusa sisitemu ari izawe cyangwa ufitiye uruhushya rwanditse; gusuzuma nta ruhushya bishobora kunyuranya n'amategeko."),
      ("Watetezi hutumia zana tofauti kwa kazi tofauti: SIEM na uchambuzi wa kumbukumbu (Splunk, Elastic/ELK, Wazuh, OSSEC, IBM QRadar, Microsoft Sentinel), ulinzi na mwitikio wa vifaa (CrowdStrike, Microsoft Defender, Velociraptor kwa uchunguzi), usimamizi wa kesi na mwitikio (TheHive, SOAR) na kujaribu programu (OWASP ZAP, Burp Suite; sqlmap hujaribu SQL injection kwenye mifumo unayoruhusiwa kujaribu).", "Zana husaidia lakini hazichukui nafasi ya ujuzi na mchakato. Jaribu mifumo unayomiliki tu au yenye ruhusa ya maandishi; uchunguzi usioruhusiwa unaweza kuwa kinyume cha sheria.")),
]
